<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goldene Aue</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Golden Meadow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Goldene Aue ('Golden Meadow') is a fertile lowland in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> between the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> and the Kyffhäuser hills, drained by the Helme and divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>. Its rich farmland around Nordhausen and Sangerhausen was held in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> by the counts of Hohnstein, Stolberg and Schwarzburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goldene-aue.jpg" alt="Goldene Aue" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DemocraticLuntz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lafourche_Parish_Louisiana_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Golden_Meadow_Highlighted.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
